course: dictionary
lesson: 11655
title: One word, three meanings: Aryan
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word «Aryan» is a good example. Long ago it was an old name for a group of ancient people, and in Sanskrit «arya» meant «noble». Read the sentences around the word to find out which meaning is being used.
explain: «The Aryan people spoke early languages in Iran and northern India.» Here Aryan is a history word about ancient people. Be careful, though. Later, the Nazis in Germany misused the word to mean a made-up «master race». That idea was false and cruel, and it was used to justify the Holocaust. Historians explain this clearly and do not use the word in that way.
explain: «Aryan» is also a boy's name in India and other places. Like «Aarya» or «Arian», it is a name, and a name is written with a capital letter. When you meet a hard word, ask: is this a name, an old history word, or a word with a cruel past? The sentences will show you.
fact: Aryan was an old name for ancient people who spoke early Indo-Iranian languages in Iran and northern India.
fact: «Arya» meant «noble» in Sanskrit, an ancient language.
fact: The Nazis misused «Aryan» to mean a made-up «master race». This idea was false and cruel.
fact: Scientists today say «Indo-European» or «Indo-Iranian» for the languages, because «Aryan» is no longer used that way.
fact: Aryan (also spelled Aarya or Arian) is also a boy's name in India and elsewhere.
exercise: «The Aryan people spoke early languages in Iran and northern India.» What does Aryan name here? | A river in Germany | A made-up master race | *An ancient group of people who spoke early Indo-Iranian languages | A type of castle
exercise: In Sanskrit, «arya» meant what? | Fast | Dark | *Noble | Lost
exercise: The Nazis used «Aryan» for a made-up master race. Why is this idea wrong? | It only described hair colour, so it was harmless | It was a kind and fair idea | It was proven by scientists in Germany | *It was false and cruel, and used to justify the Holocaust
test: Aryan is also a boy's name in India. What kind of word is it in that sentence? | A kind of language | *A name | A verb | A river
test: Today, what do scientists say instead of «Aryan» for the languages? | *Indo-European or Indo-Iranian | Sanskrit only | Aryan languages | Nazi languages
exam: Why do historians say the Nazi use of «Aryan» was wrong? | *Because the idea of a master race was false and cruel | Because the word means fast in Sanskrit | Because Aryan is only a boy's name | Because the Nazis were the first people to speak Sanskrit
